QcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788315230992955001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_lib_identity.py:105` retains `rebar.create_placeholder(...)` as a compatibility alias for `rebar.ensure_identity_for(...)` and `_commands.identity.ensure_identity_for`. The maintainer approved removal of all Python/MCP operation aliases.\n\n## Approach\n\nMigrate every repository consumer, documentation example, dynamic reference, and monkeypatch target to `ensure_identity_for`, then delete the old public alias and export. Record the intentional pre-1.0 break and preserve the canonical identity result/error behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_lib_identity.py`, public exports, and canonical identity command\n- docs/examples/changelog and Python API tests\n- static, string, dynamic, and monkeypatch consumers\n\n## Testing\n\nAssert the old alias is absent/rejected at the Python boundary; run canonical identity creation, existing-identity, and validation-failure controls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `create_placeholder` is absent from public Python exports, docs, examples, and repository consumers.\n- [ ] Every former consumer uses `ensure_identity_for` and its canonical command owner.\n- [ ] The canonical operation preserves identity creation, existing-identity, and validation-failure behavior.\n- [ ] Changelog/release material identifies the pre-1.0 breaking replacement and focused identity tests pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_identity.py","reason":"remove create_placeholder forwarding alias"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/identity.py","reason":"canonical ensure_identity_for owner"},{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"remove public alias export"},{"path":"docs","reason":"migrate Python API exampl